From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ethan Hill <ethan.hill1999@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:05:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] CandyOS P26: replace the boot animation with the spinning
 candy wordmark

vendor/lineage/bootanimation/ generates bootanimation.zip at build time
from a committed frame tar; CandyOS swaps the content for the CandyOS
wordmark from assets/CandyOSwordswhite.svg - the candy disc spins
clockwise in place while the "CandyOS" text stays static - and reworks
the movie geometry for it (the stock 3:1 band is the LineageOS wordmark
layout; the renderer draws the desc W x H quad centered on any screen):

* bootanimation.tar: 90 frames rendered from the SVG with the Roboto
  2013 family the ROM pins (scripts/candyos-gen-bootanimation.py
  regenerates it deterministically; fonts bundled in assets/fonts/).
  The canvas is the wordmark content box padded to a 6:1 aspect, so the
  wordmark renders centered at ~75% of the screen width instead of
  touching the display edges (user QA on the emulator found the original
  edge-to-edge fit too tight). part0, 30 frames: the whole wordmark
  fades in from black while the candy starts to spin; part1, 60 frames:
  one full revolution at full alpha.
* desc.txt: "c 1 0 part0" (intro plays once, always completes) then
  "f 0 0 part1 30" (loop until boot completes, then fade out over 30
  frames while the spin continues).
* Android.mk: IMAGEHEIGHT/IMAGESCALEHEIGHT = width / 6 (the 6:1 wordmark
  movie; 6 divides 720/1080/1440/2160 exactly, and the canvas is built
  to exactly 6:1 so the desc quad never stretches the frames), and
  mogrify drops "-colors 256": the frames ship pre-quantized from the
  generator, and per-frame palette re-quantization made the static text
  edges shimmer (each frame's palette is optimized for that frame's
  spinning disc, so shared text pixels remapped slightly differently).

60 fps, 6 degrees per frame: one revolution per second, continuous
across the part0 -> part1 seam (174 -> 180 degrees) and the part1 loop
wrap (534 -> 180). Fully transparent pixels are zeroed to black so the
build-time resize antialiases the glyphs against the black background
uniformly.

Change-Id: I50c2ec50681b809df52b57b965cd5a46a5dd5748
---
 bootanimation/Android.mk        |   6 +++---
 bootanimation/bootanimation.tar | Bin 6430720 -> 7106560 bytes
 bootanimation/desc.txt          |   3 +--
 3 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bootanimation/Android.mk b/bootanimation/Android.mk
index 97948f38..a9d460b0 100644
--- a/bootanimation/Android.mk
+++ b/bootanimation/Android.mk
@@ -28,13 +28,13 @@ $(TARGET_GENERATED_BOOTANIMATION): $(SOONG_ZIP)
 	    IMAGEWIDTH=$(TARGET_SCREEN_WIDTH); \
 	fi; \
 	IMAGESCALEWIDTH=$$IMAGEWIDTH; \
-	IMAGESCALEHEIGHT=$$(expr $$IMAGESCALEWIDTH / 3); \
+	IMAGESCALEHEIGHT=$$(expr $$IMAGESCALEWIDTH / 6); \
 	if [ "$(TARGET_BOOTANIMATION_HALF_RES)" = "true" ]; then \
 	    IMAGEWIDTH="$$(expr "$$IMAGEWIDTH" / 2)"; \
 	fi; \
-	IMAGEHEIGHT=$$(expr $$IMAGEWIDTH / 3); \
+	IMAGEHEIGHT=$$(expr $$IMAGEWIDTH / 6); \
 	RESOLUTION="$$IMAGEWIDTH"x"$$IMAGEHEIGHT"; \
-	prebuilts/tools-lineage/${HOST_OS}-x86/bin/mogrify -resize $$RESOLUTION -colors 256 $(INTERMEDIATES)/*/*.png; \
+	prebuilts/tools-lineage/${HOST_OS}-x86/bin/mogrify -resize $$RESOLUTION $(INTERMEDIATES)/*/*.png; \
 	echo "$$IMAGESCALEWIDTH $$IMAGESCALEHEIGHT 60" > $(INTERMEDIATES)/desc.txt; \
 	cat vendor/lineage/bootanimation/desc.txt >> $(INTERMEDIATES)/desc.txt
 	$(hide) $(SOONG_ZIP) -L 0 -o $@ -C $(INTERMEDIATES) -D $(INTERMEDIATES)
diff --git a/bootanimation/bootanimation.tar b/bootanimation/bootanimation.tar
index 14d5606215d77b922ab9047fdf71e7d464bb1513..a472bbea5de2007a9100dcb95d2c6be03b0e6caa 100644
